! The ten-site silicon supercell of `si10-nc.in` with a **PBE** norm-conserving
! dataset, so that the gradient correction is exercised at ten sites and on a
! cell whose symmetry group needed the metric bound to be found at all
! (`gradcorr` runs on the symmetrised density, so a missing operation moves it
! too). Everything but the pseudopotential and the cutoff is `si10-nc.in`'s.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 0, celldm(1) = 10.20, nat = 10, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 18.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
CELL_PARAMETERS alat
  -0.50  0.00  0.50
   0.00  0.50  0.50
  -2.50  2.50  0.00
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pbe-rrkj.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si    0.0000    0.0000    0.0000
 Si    0.2500    0.2500    0.2500
 Si   -0.5000    0.5000    0.0000
 Si   -0.2500    0.7500    0.2500
 Si   -1.0000    1.0000    0.0000
 Si   -0.7500    1.2500    0.2500
 Si   -1.5000    1.5000    0.0000
 Si   -1.2500    1.7500    0.2500
 Si   -2.0000    2.0000    0.0000
 Si   -1.7500    2.2500    0.2500
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 1 0 0 0
